{"context": "A research team is analyzing the failure modes of a trained monitor compared to prompted frontier monitors on out-of-distribution datasets. On one dataset, training increased the rate at which the monitor flags benign trajectories as scheming, and the cause of this increase is not yet clear.\n\nQuestion: How should the team interpret the increase in false positives on that dataset after training?", "options": ["Read the increase in false positives as training widening the monitor's suspicion, so that ordinary mistakes and incompetence in trajectories get flagged as scheming.", "Test whether the flagged trajectories share a dataset artifact by running the trained monitor on ablated versions lacking the scheming signal before trusting the headline rate."], "principles": [], "persona": "An AI safety researcher or technical forecaster who prizes epistemic rigor, precise conceptual distinctions, and methodological soundness. They insist on clear definitional boundaries—scheming vs. reward hacking, distinct task capabilities vs. single capability estimates—over tidy collapsible taxonomies. They favor theory-first reasoning (coverage claims need defined criteria) paired with concrete, mechanism-focused empirical evidence over speculative arguments. They are scope-disciplined: they prefer tractable, well-founded analyses over ambitious extensions built on noisy inputs, and conservative, hedged forecasts that flag model limitations over confident headline numbers. On alignment risk, they take deceptive alignment seriously as an incentive-structure concern while remaining cautious about unproven claims, favoring layered defenses (control, interpretability, oversight), mechanism-aware measurement, and mitigations that don't merely train models to hide the measured signal. They distrust lab-to-deployment extrapolation, preferring real-world data even if noisy. They are skeptical of low-evidence-value experiments with confounded interpretations, preferring controlled baselines, non-IID generalization tests, and diagnostics that cleanly distinguish hypotheses. They value conceptual generality (architecture-agnostic interpretability, universal learning dynamics) and calm, accessible public communication.", "past_choices": []}
